# Line endings, settled once.
#
# Everything here is written by a tool: the build writes the pages, the readers
# write the data files, and all of them write LF. On Windows git checks the
# same files out as CRLF by default, so the moment anybody rebuilt, git called
# a dozen files modified that were byte for byte what was already committed.
#
# Stored LF, checked out LF, on every machine. Editors have coped with this for
# twenty years; a phantom diff after every build is harder to live with.
* text=auto eol=lf

# And the ones that are not text at all, so nothing goes near their bytes.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.bin binary
*.etl binary
